## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/possample.html
- Summary (EN): The Position Sample node reads values from a texture by looking up each pixel or voxel's position. It takes the world-space position in one input and fetches the matching value from another. The output, named sample, has the same shape as the pos input.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Position Sample lit une texture à partir des positions monde d'une première entrée, et renvoie un résultat de même forme que pos.

- Inputs meaning: ["pos: RGB layer, vector VDB or vector attribute giving the world-space position to look up", "texture: layer or VDB from which values are read"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source; the only documented parameter"]

- Caveats: ["The page gives no further parameter detail.", "Related nodes: Position Map and UV Sample."]

